    "body": "## Summary\n\nFinal commit of ADR-058. Marks the ADR as Implemented with a **production-verified delta** — the strongest verification category.\n\n## The verified delta\n\n**Screenshot 2026-11-02, Wikipedia HTML article:**\n\n| Element | Before ADR-058 | After ADR-058 |\n|---|---|---|\n| Search magnifier | `y=7` (container top) | **`y=18` (centered)** |\n| Wikipedia logo | correct | correct |\n| Body / layout | correct | correct |\n\n**The 5-ADR magnifier chain closes with visible production proof:**\n\n| ADR | Contribution | Icon y |\n|---|---|---|\n| 054 | Diagnose `top: 50%` + `translateY(-50%)` | invisible |\n| 055 | `background:` color forms | invisible |\n| 056 | `background:` URL forms — **renders** | 7 |\n| 057 | `parent_content_height` threading | 7 |\n| **058** | **`top: 50%` + `translateY(-50%)`** | **18 (centered)** |\n\n## The perf split-timer measurement (ADR-059 foundation)\n\n**Release build, Wikipedia HTML article:**\n\n```\nPERF-CASCADE: 1057.9ms  PERF-LAYOUT: 2379.3ms  PERF-TOTAL: 3437.2ms\n```\n\n| Phase | Time | % |\n|---|---|---|\n| Cascade | 1058ms | 31% |\n| Layout | 2379ms | 69% |\n| **Total** | **3437ms** | 100% |\n\n**Debug build:** 10,544ms total. Release speedup is ~3.1x — expected for `-O0` → `-O2`. **Not a build-flags-only problem; the underlying work is genuinely expensive.**\n\nBoth halves are O(n²)-ish:\n- Cascade: selector matching has no indexing (rules × elements)\n- Layout: 48 `style->get()` calls per element with string keys\n\nADR-059 (perf cycle) uses this data as its Context.\n\n## Why the split-timer is part of ADR-058's scope\n\nIt lives in the same `render_pipeline.cpp` that ADR-058's Commit 1 already touched. It's permanent measurement infrastructure that ADR-059 relies on. Shipping it as ADR-058's Commit 2 keeps the ledger clean: **the ADR that discovered the need for measurement is the same one that ships the measurement.**\n\n## What this PR carries\n\n- ADR-058 → Implemented (production-verified: magnifier centered)\n- Post-ADR-058 note in ADR-054 (chain closes; ADR-054's translateY deferral satisfied)\n- Post-ADR-058 note in ADR-056 (the icon ADR-056 made visible is now centered)\n- Post-ADR-058 note in ADR-057 (second consumer of `parent_content_height`; the field's design held up)\n- README row + CHANGELOG entry\n\n## Honest notes on the session's discipline\n\n**Definition-body split-declaration discipline applied twice.** ADR-057 hit this (missing .cpp definitions after .hpp declaration updates). ADR-058 avoided it by explicitly patching both `paint.cpp` wrapper + restore lines in the same patch and verifying via `did_rotate` grep.\n\n**The two-layer structure is a genuine CSS-spec distinction, not an implementation choice.** `top: %` uses parent height; `translateY(-50%)` uses own height. Attempting one unified resolution would use the wrong reference for one of them.\n\n**The magnifier centering formula was documented by ADR-054** (`7 + 21 - 10 = 18`) — six ADRs before the chain completed. ADR-058 wasn't guessing at the target; it was shipping a formula that ADR-054 had already derived from measurement.\n\n## Test count\n\n- 669 → 675 cases (+6, 1 flipped)\n- 2562 → 2586 assertions (+24)\n- Documentation only; no code changes in this PR\n\nRefs #255\n",
